---
import MainContainer from "../components/MainContainer.astro"
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"

const pageTitle = "Colophon"
const description = "How this site is put together."

const swatches = [
  { token: "background", note: "page" },
  { token: "card", note: "raised surface" },
  { token: "muted", note: "hover, pills" },
  { token: "border", note: "hairlines" },
  { token: "foreground", note: "ink" },
  { token: "muted-foreground", note: "secondary ink" },
  { token: "links", note: "link text" },
  { token: "accent", note: "oxide" },
]
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle} description={description}>
  <MainContainer>
    <div class="prose max-w-none colophon">
      <h2 id="stack">Stack</h2>
      <p>
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, styled with <a href="https://tailwindcss.com/">Tailwind CSS v4</a>, with a little <a href="https://svelte.dev/">Svelte</a> for search and view counts. Hosted on <a href="https://vercel.com">Vercel</a>. Comments run on <a href="https://giscus.app/">Giscus</a>, which stores them in GitHub Discussions. Page views live in <a href="https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/astro-db/">Astro DB</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="typography">Typography</h2>
      <p>
        Headings and interface text are set in <a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Archivo" style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 118">Archivo</a>, a grotesque with a width axis. Headings use it wide (118%), the nav uses it at normal width. Body copy is <a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Source+Serif+4" style="font-family: var(--font-body)">Source Serif 4</a>, chosen because it has an optical-size axis and holds up at 18px on a phone. Code is <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/"><code>JetBrains Mono</code></a>. All three are variable fonts served from this domain via <a href="https://fontsource.org/">Fontsource</a>, so nothing is fetched from Google.
      </p>

      <h2 id="color">Colour</h2>
      <p>
        The palette is one cool graphite ramp (OKLCH hue 240 to 255) and a single oxide orange. The orange is a nod to surveyor's paint and rebar from my civil engineering years. Light and dark themes share the same hues; dark mode raises lightness and nudges chroma up so the orange doesn't go muddy. Everything is defined in OKLCH with <code>light-dark()</code>, and every text colour clears WCAG AA in both themes.
      </p>
      <ul class="swatches">
        {
          swatches.map((swatch) => (
            <li style={`--swatch: var(--${swatch.token})`}>
              <span class="chip" />
              <code>--{swatch.token}</code>
              <span class="note">{swatch.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <h2 id="feedback">Sound and haptics</h2>
      <p>
        Clicking anything on this site makes a small sound and, on phones that allow it, a small buzz. The sound is a 14 millisecond burst of filtered noise synthesised in the browser with Web Audio, so there are no audio files to download. I tried a packaged UI sound library first, but its shortest click was ten times longer and sounded like a notification. The buzz comes from <a href="https://github.com/lochie/web-haptics">web-haptics</a>. It works on Android and on iOS before 26.5; Apple closed the loophole it relied on after that. The speaker icon in the header mutes both, and the choice is remembered.
      </p>

      <h2 id="source">Source</h2>
      <p>
        The whole thing is on <a href="https://github.com/bhekanik/bhekani.com">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </MainContainer>

  <style>
    .swatches {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: var(--space-6) 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
    }
    .swatches li {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto auto 1fr;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-3);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .chip {
      width: 1.75rem;
      height: 1.75rem;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      background: var(--swatch);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .swatches code {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }
    .note {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      color: var(--muted-foreground);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
